[[Image:ingame Transarent Blocks|thumb|How transparent blocks behave.]] There are a few blocks in the game that are both transparent to light and can have [[Redstone Wire]] placed on them.
==List of these blocks== {|class=wikitable !Block!!State |- |{{Block|Glowstone}} || Any |- |{{Block|Stone Slab}}|| Top-half (bit 0x8 on) |- |{{Block|Sandstone Slab}}|| Top-half (bit 0x8 on) |- |{{Block|Wooden Slab}}|| Top-half (bit 0x8 on) |- |{{Block|Cobblestone Slab}}|| Top-half (bit 0x8 on) |- |{{Block|Brick Slab}}|| Top-half (bit 0x8 on) |- |{{Block|Stone Brick Slab}}|| Top-half (bit 0x8 on) |- |{{Block|Oak Wood Slab}}|| Top-half (bit 0x8 on) |- |{{Block|Spruce Wood Slab}}|| Top-half (bit 0x8 on) |- |{{Block|Birch Wood Slab}}|| Top-half (bit 0x8 on) |- |{{Block|Jungle Wood Slab}}|| Top-half (bit 0x8 on) |- |{{Block|Wooden Stairs}}|| Upside-Down (bit 0x4 on) |- |{{Block|Cobblestone Stairs}}|| Upside-Down (bit 0x4 on) |- |{{Block|Brick Stairs}}|| Upside-Down (bit 0x4 on) |- |{{Block|Stone Brick Stairs}}|| Upside-Down (bit 0x4 on) |- |{{Block|Nether Brick Stairs}}|| Upside-Down (bit 0x4 on) |- |{{Block|Sandstone Stairs}}|| Upside-Down (bit 0x4 on) |- |}
==Behavior== *[[Image:ingame Wire On Slabs|thumb|Some wire on top of a transparent block]] Wire can be placed on top of them and signal will travel across it normally *[[Image:ingame Pinch Examples.png|thumb|Image showing how certain blocks don't pinch wire]] They do not pinch wire when it's traveling up or down a staircase and you place them above it, and signal will travel normally. *[[Image:ingame Slab downward signal.png|thumb|Signal does not go directly down off a transparent block]] Signal will travel up onto a slab, but not down directly off of it.

