A redstone device is said to be ''tileable'' when multiple exact copies of itself can be placed next to eachother with no space in between.
== See Also == * [[Flush]]
{{stub}}

A redstone device is said to be ''tileable'' when multiple exact copies of itself can be placed next to eachother with no space in between and still work as expected. Some tileable machines have a different, yet intended behavior when placed next to eachother, such as working in sync with one another.
== See Also == * [[Flush]]
{{stub}}

A redstone device is said to be ''flush'' when it can be constructed exactly 1 block wide. with no extruding parts. Many flush redstone devices are also [[tileable]].
== See Also == * [[Tileable]]
{{stub}}

